  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "An arithmetic series has the first term ${a}_{1}=5$, the second term is ${a}_{2}=15$, and the sum of the series is ${S}_{N}=845.$ Find the number of terms $N$ in the series.",
  "worked_solution": "To solve this problem, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series.\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d)\n$$\n\nSince we know the first two terms of the arithmetic series, we can find its common difference, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={a}_{2}-{a}_{1} \\\\  & =15-5 \\\\  & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting ${a}_{1}=5$, $d=10$, and ${S}_{N}=845$ into the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d) \\\\ 845 & =\\frac{N}{2}(2(5)+(N-1)(10)) \\\\ 845 & =\\frac{N}{2}(10+10N-10) \\\\ 845 & =\\frac{N}{2}(10N) \\\\ 845 & =5{N}^{2} \\\\ 169 & ={N}^{2} \\\\ N & =13\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we take the positive square root because $N$ can't be negative.",
